# Build and run context.
#
# Everything the image actually needs is kept; everything a person would rather
# not have in an image is kept out. In particular tests/ is excluded: a failing
# test in a demo image is noise, and the suite is run on the host or in CI.

.git
.gitignore
.github
.venv
venv
__pycache__
**/__pycache__
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache
.coverage
htmlcov
.mypy_cache
.ruff_cache

tests/
docs/
CONTEXT.md
AGENTS.md
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# The sample data is copied in explicitly, so the working tree copy of it is
# ignored here to keep the context small.
data/*.db
data/*.sqlite
data/*.sqlite3

# README.md is deliberately absent from this list. pyproject.toml declares it as
# the distribution's long description, so pip needs it during the install, and
# excluding it here made `COPY pyproject.toml README.md ./` fail with a missing
# file. Dockerfile, docker-compose.yml and .dockerignore stay out: they are not
# part of the image.
Dockerfile
docker-compose.yml
.dockerignore
